#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

usage() {
    cat <<'HELP'
Usage: wrap-up [--date YYYY-MM-DD] -- 'Title' < handover.org
       wrap-up --help

The wrap-up slot: keep a session's handover, in the ClankOS container.
This image fills it with pos-wrap-up, which seals the handover, read
from standard input, in the working directory's archive, adds its
heading to the working directory's journal.org tagged handover and
latest, and prints the record's citation, the title and the date.
"clankos-run help wrap-up" prints the protocol.

    wrap-up -- 'The roof mended' < handover.org
    ipfs://bafkrei...: The roof mended, 2030-03-04

The title is one nonempty line. The date is today unless --date gives
another. Refused if the handover is empty, the date is not written
YYYY-MM-DD, journal.org is locked by an editor, or the archive refuses
the seal.

Exit: 0 kept, 1 refused, its reason on stderr, 2 usage, 255 Emacs
error; 125, 126 and 127 are clankos-run's.
HELP
}

case "${1:-}" in
    ''|help|-h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
esac
exec "$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/clankos-run" wrap-up "$@"
